      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Pityriasis lichenoides et varioliformis acuta (PLEVA) is a common inflammatory disease which usually occurs in children and young adults. Characteristic is a polymorph clinical picture with papules, erosions, ulcers and haemorrhagic crusts compatible with many differential diagnoses. We report about a patient with PLEVA and describe possible differential diagnoses."},
